---
interface Props { compact?: boolean }
const { compact = false } = Astro.props;
const github = "https://github.com/mithudso/github-explorer";
const release = `${github}/releases/tag/v0.4.2`;
const npmArchive = `${github}/releases/download/v0.4.2/mitchphudson-github-explorer-0.4.2.tgz`;
const shortcuts = [
  ["F1", "Status", "git status --short --branch"], ["F2", "Pull", "git pull --ff-only"],
  ["F3", "Push", "git push"], ["F4", "Fetch", "git fetch"],
  ["F5", "Diff", "git diff"], ["F6", "Stage interactively", "git add --patch"],
  ["F7", "Commit", "git commit"], ["F8", "Create a PR", "gh pr create"],
  ["F9", "Check out a PR", "gh pr checkout"], ["F10", "Merge a PR", "gh pr merge"],
  ["F11", "List PRs", "gh pr list"], ["F12", "PR checks", "gh pr checks"],
];
---
<section id="github-explorer" class:list={["github-explorer", { compact }]} aria-labelledby="github-explorer-heading">
  <p class="eyebrow">Terminal workbench · macOS &amp; Linux · MIT</p>
  <h2 id="github-explorer-heading">GitHub Explorer</h2>
  <p class="ghx-intro">Your repository, Vim and GitHub CLI in one terminal.</p>
  <p>
    Browse your checkout, edit and save files in real embedded Vim, change repository settings,
    and run Git and GitHub commands from a searchable interface. Keep your current branch,
    changed-file count, open pull requests and other branches in view while you work.
  </p>
  <figure>
    <a href="/images/github-explorer/editor.png" aria-label="Open full-size GitHub Explorer editor screenshot">
      <img src="/images/github-explorer/editor.png" width="1726" height="1124" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
        alt="GitHub Explorer showing repository files on the left, README open in embedded Vim on the right, action buttons and branch status below." />
    </a>
    <figcaption>GitHub Explorer 0.4.1 editing its own public repository. Select the image to see it full size.</figcaption>
  </figure>
  <pre><code>{`brew install mithudso/tap/github-explorer
gh auth login
github-explorer --cwd ~/dev/my-project`}</code></pre>
  <p class="ghx-links">
    <a class="btn" href={compact ? "/downloads/#github-explorer" : "#github-explorer-setup"}>Install &amp; set up</a>
    <a class="btn secondary" href={github}>Source on GitHub</a>
    <a href={release}>Download v0.4.2</a>
    {compact && <a href="/downloads/#github-explorer-usage">Usage &amp; options</a>}
  </p>
  {compact ? (
    <p class="ghx-note">Homebrew installs the required tools. Python and npm-tarball installation, screenshots,
      all launch options and keyboard shortcuts are on the <a href="/downloads/#github-explorer">Downloads page</a>.</p>
  ) : (
    <>
      <div class="ghx-features">
        <div><h3>Files and Vim</h3><p>Search tracked and untracked files above the command tree. A selected local text file opens in Vim in the right pane, with its normal modes and save commands. Remote repositories without a matching checkout have read-only previews.</p></div>
        <div><h3>The installed CLI, discoverable</h3><p>Search the commands available in your installed <code>gh</code>, including PRs, issues, Actions, releases and extensions. Add flags and arguments or edit the command directly. The local Git menu includes pull, push, fetch, commit, merge and branch switching.</p></div>
        <div><h3>Repository settings</h3><p>Open <strong>Repo settings</strong> to see options from <code>gh repo edit --help</code>. Available current values are prefilled. Check only the fields you want to change, then review the command and target repository before applying.</p></div>
        <div><h3>Visible state and explicit actions</h3><p>The status bar keeps the current branch, distinct changed files, open PRs and other branches visible. Open its details for PR links and branch names. Hide the action rows for more space. Every Git/GitHub action previews its command and context before execution.</p></div>
      </div>
      <figure>
        <a href="/images/github-explorer/commands.png" aria-label="Open full-size GitHub Explorer command screenshot">
          <img src="/images/github-explorer/commands.png" width="1726" height="1124" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
            alt="GitHub Explorer command interface with git pull selected, its command preview and help, repository files and twelve shortcut buttons." />
        </a>
        <figcaption>Search commands, inspect their help, then choose Run or Terminal. Nothing runs just because you select it.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <h3 id="github-explorer-setup">Installation and setup</h3>
      <p><strong>Homebrew:</strong> use the command above on macOS or Linux with Homebrew. The author's
        <a href="https://github.com/mithudso/homebrew-tap/blob/main/Formula/github-explorer.rb">tap formula</a>
        installs GitHub CLI, Git, Vim and Python in addition to an isolated application environment.</p>
      <p><strong>npm:</strong> requires Node.js 18+, <a href="https://docs.astral.sh/uv/getting-started/installation/">uv</a>,
        <a href="https://cli.github.com/">GitHub CLI</a>, Git and Vim on PATH. Install the release tarball below while npm processes the submitted
        <code>@mitchphudson/github-explorer</code> registry package. The launcher bundles the Python application and uses uv
        to install its pinned dependencies in a cached environment. First launch needs network access.</p>
      <pre><code>{`npm install -g ${npmArchive}

gh auth login
ghx --cwd ~/dev/my-project`}</code></pre>
      <p>You can also <a href={npmArchive}>download the npm tarball</a> from the GitHub release.</p>
      <p><strong>Python / uv:</strong> Python 3.11+ is supported. With GitHub CLI, Git and Vim available, install the tagged source:</p>
      <pre><code>{`uv tool install git+https://github.com/mithudso/github-explorer.git@v0.4.2
ghx --cwd ~/dev/my-project`}</code></pre>
      <p>Run from an existing checkout, or clone one first with <code>gh repo clone OWNER/REPO</code>.
        Authenticate once with <code>gh auth login</code>; the app uses your existing GitHub CLI configuration.
        A terminal around 120 columns × 40 rows or larger is comfortable. Both <code>github-explorer</code>
        and <code>ghx</code> launch the same app.</p>
      <h3 id="github-explorer-usage">Usage and launch options</h3>
      <pre><code>{`# Open the repository in your current directory
ghx

# Select a checkout explicitly
ghx --cwd ~/dev/my-project

# Browse a GitHub repository (read-only files without a matching checkout)
ghx --repo OWNER/REPO

# GitHub Enterprise context
ghx --cwd ~/dev/my-project --repo github.example.com/OWNER/REPO

# Inspect the locally discovered command catalog without opening the TUI
ghx --list-commands`}</code></pre>
      <div class="ghx-table"><table>
        <caption>All launch options</caption>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Option</th><th scope="col">Behavior</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><code>--cwd PATH</code></td><td>Repository working directory; defaults to where you launch the app.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>--repo [HOST/]OWNER/REPO</code></td><td>Override the GitHub repository. Local Git commands still target the selected working directory.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>--list-commands</code></td><td>Print the installed gh command catalog as JSON and exit.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>--version</code></td><td>Print the installed application version.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>-h, --help</code></td><td>Show launch help and exit.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table></div>
      <h3>Editing and navigation</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Select a local text file to enter Vim. Press <kbd>i</kbd> to insert, <kbd>Esc</kbd> to return to normal mode, <code>:w</code> to save, or <code>:wq</code> to save and close. <kbd>Ctrl+S</kbd> and the Save button also request a save; inspect Vim for any write error.</li>
        <li>Vim keeps its unsaved-buffer prompts when changing files or closing. Close Vim before running Git commands. <kbd>Ctrl+\</kbd> moves focus back to the file tree.</li>
        <li>Use arrows to navigate the TUI. Down expands a collapsed tree branch, then moves through its children. Inputs and dropdowns retain their editing and selection keys.</li>
        <li>Use Hide actions / Show actions, or <kbd>Ctrl+B</kbd> outside Vim, to toggle the bottom controls. The repository status bar remains visible. When Vim has focus, it receives its normal navigation and function keys.</li>
        <li><strong>Run</strong> captures command output and supports Stop and a configurable timeout. <strong>Terminal</strong> suspends the TUI for interactive commands, editors and authentication, then returns you to the workbench.</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>Common commands: buttons and hotkeys</h3>
      <p>These shortcuts open a confirmation with the working directory, repository and command.
        PR creation, checkout, merging, staging and committing use the terminal for interactive input.</p>
      <div class="ghx-table"><table>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Key</th><th scope="col">Action</th><th scope="col">Command</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>{shortcuts.map(([key, label, command]) => <tr><td><kbd>{key}</kbd></td><td>{label}</td><td><code>{command}</code></td></tr>)}</tbody>
      </table></div>
      <p class="ghx-links"><a href={`${github}#readme`}>Full README and troubleshooting</a>
        <a href={release}>Release files and SHA-256 checksums</a>
        <a href={`${github}/issues`}>Report an issue</a></p>
    </>
  )}
</section>

<style>
  .github-explorer { scroll-margin-top: 12rem; margin: 2.5rem 0; padding: 1.5rem; border: 1px solid var(--line-strong); border-radius: 12px; }
  .github-explorer h2 { margin-top: 0; }
  .ghx-intro { font-size: 1.3rem; font-weight: 600; }
  .ghx-links { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: .8rem 1.2rem; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  figure { margin: 1.5rem 0; }
  img { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid var(--line-strong); }
  figcaption, .ghx-note { font-size: .9rem; color: var(--ink-muted); }
  figcaption { margin-top: .6rem; }
  .ghx-features { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: .5rem 2rem; }
  .ghx-table { overflow-x: auto; }
  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; }
  th, td { padding: .65rem; text-align: left; vertical-align: top; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-strong); }
  caption { text-align: left; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: .5rem; }
  pre { max-width: 100%; overflow-x: auto; }
  kbd { font-family: monospace; white-space: nowrap; }
  h3[id] { scroll-margin-top: 5rem; }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .github-explorer { padding: 1rem; }
    .ghx-features { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .ghx-table { font-size: .85rem; }
  }
</style>
